{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"demoniac-androgenic-queenbee","creation_channel":"python","description":"# J3 — Pin a `RichTextCodec` contract (ADF for Cloud, wiki/plain text for Data Center)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nRich-text encoding is one of the three real differences between Jira Cloud and Data Center: Cloud's REST v3\nrequires Atlassian Document Format (a nested JSON document; sending a plain string returns 400), while DC's\nREST v2 carries descriptions and comment bodies as plain text / wiki markup. Today ADF is hardwired into the\nCloud path — `adapters/jira/adf.py` provides `fit_text_to_adf_limit` and the decode, and\n`adapters/jira/backend.py:42-72`'s `map_fields_to_remote` calls `outbound_fields._load_adf()` inline. PR #120's\nanswer was to copy that whole method and change the single ADF line, which is the duplication this epic exists\nto prevent.\n\n## Approach\n\nDefine a `RichTextCodec` Protocol in `adapters/jira_family/` [rebar:62d9-9f6d-ecf4-4743] with two operations: `fit_outbound`\n(fit a local string to the deployment's rich-text limit, returning the deployment's wire shape) and\n`decode_inbound` (turn a wire body into plain text). Provide two implementations — `AdfCodec`, which delegates\nto the existing `adapters/jira/adf.py` with no logic change, and `WikiTextCodec`, a character-count fit plus an\nidentity decode.\n\nThe shared `map_fields_to_remote` then takes the codec as a constructor dependency, so exactly one\nimplementation of the mapping exists and the ADF-vs-wiki difference is a parameter. The same codec is the\ndependency J2 [rebar:62d9-9f6d-ecf4-4743] injects into the relocated `_sanitize_description`, whose\n`fit_text_to_adf_limit` call IS this seam — so if J2 lands first with a minimal `Callable[[str], str]` fit\nfunction as a placeholder, this story widens that placeholder to the full `RichTextCodec` and re-points the\nsanitizer at it. Either landing order works; what must not happen is `jira_family/` importing the pinned\n`adapters/jira/adf.py` directly. Cloud is constructed with\n`AdfCodec` and its behavior is unchanged, proven by J1's pinned oracles [rebar:acb2-1823-2f0d-415b].\n\n**Alternative rejected:** a boolean or enum flag (`use_adf=True`) threaded through the mapper. It puts the\nbranch back inside the shared code, grows a branch per deployment type, and gives the codec no place to own its\nown limit constant.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** copying `map_fields_to_remote` per adapter (PR #120). One line differs; the other\nthirty drift.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py` (new) — the Protocol + `WikiTextCodec`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/adf.py` — wrapped by `AdfCodec`, logic unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/` — the shared mapper takes the codec.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_codec.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier for each codec (pure transforms) plus a contract test run against BOTH implementations, since the\npoint of the story is that they are interchangeable behind one Protocol.\n\n- shared contract, parameterized over both codecs: a short string round-trips through\n  `fit_outbound` → `decode_inbound` to itself; an over-limit string is fitted to at most the limit and its\n  decode is a prefix of the original.\n- Cloud-specific: `AdfCodec.fit_outbound` produces the same ADF document the current\n  `fit_text_to_adf_limit` produces for the same input — asserted against J1's pinned value.\n- DC-specific: `WikiTextCodec` truncates at its character limit and marks the truncation; `decode_inbound`\n  returns `\"\"` for `None` and passes a string through unchanged.\n- contrast case: a non-`str` value is passed through untouched by both codecs rather than coerced, matching the\n  current mapper's behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] one parameterized contract test runs against both `AdfCodec` and `WikiTextCodec` and passes for each\n- [ ] `AdfCodec` output for the J1-pinned input equals the J1-pinned expected ADF document\n- [ ] `grep -rn '_load_adf\\|fit_text_to_adf_limit' src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` shows those names\n      reached only from inside `AdfCodec`\n- [ ] exactly one definition of `map_fields_to_remote` exists in the tree","id":"a47c-44e9-bc07-4caa","parent_id":"cbca-7684-3df1-4a01","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"J3 — pin a RichTextCodec contract (ADF for Cloud, wiki/plain text for Data Center)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788224339475019001,"uuid":"b491c6a6-338b-4eb2-8723-127aca880f9e"}